# mtools 3.6: MS-DOS media, read and written from OS-9.
#
# THESE STANZAS RUN IN ORDER AND DEPEND ON EACH OTHER, and each one clears
# up after itself so the sheet can be run again and mean the same thing.
# When a regroup once sorted them alphabetically, three screens came out as
# mtools asking what to do about files a previous run had left.
#
# The image is /dd/DOS/a.img, configured as drive a: in SYS/mtools.conf.

shot    msinfo
for     msinfo mslabel msformat
cap     What the DOS floppy image is, read out of its own boot sector, and
cap     the label put on it.  msformat will NOT make one: bare it refuses
cap     non-removable media, and given the geometry it aborts on an illegal
cap     instruction.  The image that ships is the one you get.
run     /dd/CMDS/mslabel a:OS9FREEWARE
wait    10
run     /dd/CMDS/msinfo a: | /dd/CMDS/head -n 13
wait    12
run     /dd/CMDS/msformat a:
wait    12

shot    mscopy
for     mscopy msdir mstype msdel
cap     Writing two files onto the DOS disk, listing them with DOS's own
cap     8.3 names and free-space line, and reading one back.  The deletes
cap     first are what make this repeatable: mtools stops to ask before it
cap     overwrites, and a stanza that stops to ask eats the rest of its
cap     own sheet.
run     /dd/CMDS/msdel a:MOTD.TXT
wait    8
run     /dd/CMDS/mscopy /dd/SYS/motd a:MOTD.TXT
wait    10
run     /dd/CMDS/msdir a:
wait    10
run     /dd/CMDS/mstype a:MOTD.TXT
wait    10

shot    msmd
for     msmd mscd msrd msdeltree
cap     A directory made on the DOS disk, a file copied into it, and then
cap     the whole tree deleted again -- md, cd, rd and deltree, spelled the
cap     DOS way.
run     /dd/CMDS/msdeltree a:/DOCS
wait    10
run     /dd/CMDS/msmd a:/DOCS
wait    10
run     /dd/CMDS/mscopy /dd/SYS/motd a:/DOCS/README.TXT
wait    10
run     /dd/CMDS/msdir a:/DOCS
wait    10

shot    msattrib
for     msattrib
cap     A DOS attribute set and read back: R is the read-only bit, and
cap     msdir shows it.
run     /dd/CMDS/msattrib +r a:/DOCS/README.TXT
wait    10
run     /dd/CMDS/msattrib a:/DOCS/README.TXT
wait    10
run     /dd/CMDS/msdir a:/DOCS
wait    10

shot    msread
for     msread mswrite msbadblocks mstoolstest
cap     msread and mswrite are the raw pair -- a whole file in and out with
cap     none of the DOS filename rules involved.  The checksums either side
cap     show it came back unchanged.
run     /dd/CMDS/msdel a:RAW.TXT
wait    8
run     /dd/CMDS/mswrite /dd/SYS/motd a:RAW.TXT
wait    12
run     /dd/CMDS/msread a:RAW.TXT /dd/tmp/raw.out
wait    12
run     /dd/CMDS/chksum /dd/SYS/motd /dd/tmp/raw.out
wait    10

shot    mtools
for     mtools mscheck
cap     The mtools front end, listing the eighteen sub-commands that ship
cap     with it -- each one a separate program on this disk.
run     /dd/CMDS/mtools
wait    10

shot    msmove
for     msmove msren
cap     msmove asks before it overwrites, and there is no flag that stops it
cap     asking.  That is why this stanza is LAST in the sheet: a program
cap     that stops to ask reads the next commands as answers, and the rest
cap     of the sheet is gone.  Answered `q' here.
run     /dd/CMDS/msmove a:MOTD.TXT a:/
wait    10
send    q\r
wait    6


shot    dosmore
for     mscheck msinfo mslabel msdeltree
cap     msinfo reading the whole boot sector of the image that ships in
cap     /dd/DOS -- the geometry, the FAT layout, the media byte and the
cap     mformat line that would recreate it.
run     /dd/CMDS/msinfo a: | /dd/CMDS/head -n 12
wait    12
run     /dd/CMDS/mslabel a:FREEWARE
wait    10
